      "evidence": "The Definition specifies boundary charts using “the Euclidean fractional Slobodeckij space W^{1/2,2}(R^{n-1})” but gives no lower bound on n or convention for a zero-dimensional boundary. The cited dependency def-fractional-slobodeckij-space-on-euclidean-space defines its spaces only for “d≥1”; for an allowed 1D manifold, n−1=0, so the invoked space is not defined by that dependency.",
