      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "The Statement allows “a compact smooth Riemannian domain with smooth boundary” and then uses the DN maps. Its dependency def-ip-conductivity-dirichlet-to-neumann-map requires “a nonempty compact connected smooth Riemannian domain with nonempty smooth boundary.” The Statement does not exclude empty boundary; on a closed connected manifold with γ₁=γ₂=1, constants solve the conductivity equation, so its Dirichlet problem is not unique and the cited maps are not defined.",
